### MEDIUM SEVERITY ISSUES

#### Issue #6: Console Logging with System.out.println
**Severity:** MEDIUM  
**Category:** Logging & Monitoring  
**File:** `CRM-master/src/main/java/crm/csv/CSVTest.java:27`

**Problem Description:**  
Application uses `System.out.println` for logging instead of proper logging frameworks, preventing effective log aggregation in AWS CloudWatch.

**Code Location:**
```java
// Multiple occurrences in CSV processing
System.out.println(line[0] + "\t" + line[1] + "\t" + line[2]);
```

**Cloud Impact:**
- Cannot aggregate logs effectively in CloudWatch Logs
- Missing structured logging for CloudWatch Logs Insights
- No correlation IDs for distributed tracing
- Difficult to set up CloudWatch alarms
- Cannot integrate with AWS X-Ray
- Missing log levels for filtering

**AWS-Specific Remediation:**

1. **Replace with SLF4J logging:**
   ```java
   import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
   
   @Slf4j
   public class CSVTest {
       public void processCsv() {
           log.info("Processing CSV file: {}", fileName);
           log.debug("CSV line: {} - {} - {}", line[0], line[1], line[2]);
       }
   }
   ```

2. **Configure JSON logging for CloudWatch:**
   ```xml
   <!-- Add logstash-logback-encoder -->
   <dependency>
       <groupId>net.logstash.logback</groupId>
       <artifactId>logstash-logback-encoder</artifactId>
       <version>7.4</version>
   </dependency>
   ```

3. **Logback configuration:**
   ```xml
   <!-- logback-spring.xml -->
   <configuration>
       <appender name="JSON" class="ch.qos.logback.core.ConsoleAppender">
           <encoder class="net.logstash.logback.encoder.LogstashEncoder">
               <customFields>{"application":"crm","environment":"${ENVIRONMENT}"}</customFields>
           </encoder>
       </appender>
       <root level="INFO">
           <appender-ref ref="JSON"/>
       </root>
   </configuration>
   ```

4. **Add MDC for correlation tracking:**
   ```java
   MDC.put("correlationId", UUID.randomUUID().toString());
   MDC.put("userId", currentUser.getId());
   log.info("Processing request");
   ```

